import QtQml
QtObject {
    readonly property var entries: [
        { key: "overview", title: "Overview", source: "# QMarkdown playground\n\nEdit Markdown to see native Qt Quick rendering. Samples never change your settings.\n\nOpen Style controls for bounded code scrolling, wrapping, syntax palettes and task artwork. Enable individual GFM options in Style controls when needed.\n\nTry **strong**, *emphasis*, `inline code`, [host links](https://example.invalid), and denied ![image fallback](missing.png). <b>HTML stays literal</b>.\n\nSelect Nested code scrolling or GFM task lists to explore the unreleased scrolling and task presentation fixes. Native block math is opt-in.\n\n```cpp\nconst QString greeting = \"Hello, 日本語 😀\";\n```" },
        { key: "headings", title: "H1–H6 headings", source: "# H1 with `code`\n\nBody paragraph.\n\n## H2 with *emphasis*\n\n### H3 with **strong**\n\n#### H4\n\n##### H5\n\n###### H6" },
        { key: "inline", title: "Inline formatting", source: "# Inline formatting\n\n*Emphasis*, **strong**, ***both***, and `literal <b> &amp;` code.\n\nEscapes: \\*literal asterisks\\* and \\# hash.\n\nEntities: &amp; &lt; &gt; &quot; &#169; &#x1F600;\n\n## Heading with `inherited code size`" },
        { key: "code", title: "Fenced code", source: "# Fenced code\n\n``` cpp &amp;\n# Literal Markdown, <b>HTML</b> and &amp;\n  Spaces stay;\ttabs stay too.\n\nAReallyLongUnbrokenCodeLineThatWrapsInsideTheAvailablePreviewWidthWithoutHorizontalScrolling1234567890\n```\n\n~~~ text\n日本語 😀 é\n~~~\n\nEmpty fence:\n```\n```" },
        { key: "unicode", title: "Unicode and long lines", source: "# Unicode and long lines\n\né — Ελληνικά — 日本語 — 😀 🚀\n\n" + "LongUnbrokenLine1234567890".repeat(24) + "\n\n" + "A paragraph that wraps at the selected preview width. ".repeat(40) },
        { key: "leaf", title: "Core leaf blocks", source: "Setext *H1*\n===\n\nMultiline\n**H2** with `code`\n---\n\nA paragraph interrupted by a rule.\n* * *\n\n    # Literal indented code\n    <b> &amp; [link](https://example.invalid)\n\n      Residual indentation and trailing spaces  \n\n___\n\n~~~\nFenced code shares the same style.\n~~~" },
        { key: "containers", title: "Mixed containers", source: "# Native containers\n\n9) A wrapping ordered item with **strong** and `code`.\n10) Mixed children:\n    - Nested bullet\n    - > Quoted *text*\n      > with a hard break.  \n      > Next line.\n\n> ## A quoted heading\n>\n> A paragraph inside a quote.\n>\n> - Tight item\n> - Another item\n>\n> ~~~\n> literal code\n> ~~~\n\n- A loose item\n\n  A second paragraph.\n\n- Another loose item\n\n>\n\n-\n" },
        { key: "links", title: "Host-controlled links", source: "# [Linked heading](#heading)\n\n[**Strong** *emphasis* `code`](custom:action) and [empty destination]().\n\n[Reference][docs] — <https://example.invalid/a?x=1&amp;y=2> — <hello@example.invalid>\n\n[docs]: ../guide.md#intro\n\n> - [A wrapped link with a longer label to explore scrolling and hover behavior](relative/path)\n> - [![Image description](unloaded.png)](outer:link)\n\n![Inert [inner link](ignored:link)](unloaded.png)\n\n`[code](inert)` and <a href='inert'>literal HTML</a>." },
        { key: "images", title: "Images and resource policy", source: "# Native image rows\n\nImages shrink to the available width and keep their aspect ratio. This playground permits bundled qrc images only.\n\nBefore **![PNG shapes](qrc:/qmarkdown-samples/shapes.png \"Bundled PNG\")** after.\n\n> - [![JPEG shapes](qrc:/qmarkdown-samples/shapes.jpg)](sample:image)\n> - ![Denied HTTPS description](https://example.invalid/image.png)\n\n![Denied local description](file:///image.png)\n\nInline composition, SVG, animation, data URLs and HTML rendering are deferred." },
        { key: "tasks", title: "GFM task lists", source: "# GFM task lists\n\nOpen Style controls and enable GFM task lists. Compare normal and Large host task indicators, then disable Host-styled task indicators for fallback artwork. Try Task indicators replace bullets. Selection and copy should retain readable task text.\n\n- [x] **Completed** item\n- Ordinary item\n- [ ] Pending [review](task:review)\n  - [X] Nested completed item\n  - [ ] Nested pending item\n\n> 9) [ ] Quoted ordered task\n> 10) [x] Another ordered task\n\n- [ ] Loose item\n\n  A second paragraph stays inside the task.\n\n- [x] Finished\n\nEscaped markers stay literal:\n- \\[x] Ordinary item\n\n## Empty and wrapped tight tasks\n\n- [ ]\n- [x]\n- [ ] A long wrapped task label with **formatting** and `code`. A long wrapped task label with **formatting** and `code`. A long wrapped task label with **formatting** and `code`. A long wrapped task label with **formatting** and `code`. A long wrapped task label with **formatting** and `code`. A long wrapped task label with **formatting** and `code`. \n  - [ ] Nested task after wrapping\n  - Ordinary nested item\n\n1. [ ] Ordered task\n2. Ordinary ordered item\n3. [x] Completed ordered task\n" },
        { key: "strike", title: "GFM strikethrough", source: "# ~~Revised~~ heading\n\nEnable GFM strikethrough in Style controls.\n\n~Single~ and ~~double~~ delimiters; ~~~long runs~~~ stay literal.\n\n~~**Bold**, *italic*, `code` and [linked text](strike:review) compose and wrap across lines.~~\n\n- [x] ~~Completed task~~\n  - ~~Nested item~~\n- ![~~Image fallback~~](missing.png)\n\nEscaped \\~literal\\~ and `~~code~~` stay literal." },
        { key: "autolinks", title: "GFM extended autolinks", source: "# www.commonmark.org\n\nEnable GFM extended autolinks in Style controls.\n\nVisit https://commonmark.org/help and www.commonmark.org/a.b.\n\nEmail foo+tag@example.org, mailto:foo@example.org or xmpp:foo@example.org/chat@work.\n\n**www.commonmark.org** and ~~https://commonmark.org~~ inherit formatting when strikethrough is enabled.\n\n- [x] www.commonmark.org\n  - https://commonmark.org/help\n\n`www.literal.test` and [www.explicit.test](host:explicit) preserve precedence.\n\n![www.inert.test](missing.png)" },
        { key: "tables", title: "GFM tables and tag filter", source: "# GFM tables and tag filter\n\nEnable tables or All GFM in Style controls.\n\n| Left | Center | Right |\n| :--- | :---: | ---: |\n| **bold** and *emphasis* | `code` | [host link](host:table) |\n| Wrapping cell content wrapping cell content | ~~strike~~ | www.commonmark.org |\n| ![shapes](qrc:/qmarkdown-samples/shapes.png) | denied ![image](missing.png) | plain |\n| Fourth body row | More wrapped text to show column sizing and alternating backgrounds | end |\n| Fifth body row | plain | end |\n\n> | Quoted | Table |\n> | --- | --- |\n> | native | cells |\n> | nested second | wraps with available width |\n> | nested third | cells |\n\nLiteral HTML stays visible with tag filtering enabled: <title> <STYLE> <script>." },
        { key: "renderers", title: "Custom fenced renderers", source: "# Custom fenced renderers\n\nEnable Custom fences and disable Document selection to show the native preview. Re-enable selection to show selectable source.\n\n```preview full info\nThis source becomes a native QML preview.\n```\n\n> - ~~~preview\n>   Nested preview wraps with the available width.\n>   ~~~\n\n```unknown\nUnmatched language stays ordinary code.\n```" },
        { key: "reading", title: "Reading and navigation", source: "# Reading and navigation\n\nUse Find (Ctrl+F) and the heading outline. [Jump to installation](#installation), [encoded heading](#%C3%A9lan), [missing target](#missing).\n\n## Installation\n\nSearch for **reader**, `reader`, or READER.\n\n> ### Nested heading\n> reader in a quote.\n\n- #### Nested list heading\n\n## Installation\n\nDuplicate ID: [second installation](#installation-1).\n\n## Élan\n\n```preview\nreader source replaces custom visuals while Find is open.\n```" },
        { key: "keyboard", title: "Keyboard links", source: "# Keyboard links\n\nPress Tab and Shift+Tab to read links; Enter activates through the host.\n\n[First link](host:duplicate) and [same destination, separate stop](host:duplicate).\n\n> - [A long wrapped link with עברית text and an image ![shapes](qrc:/qmarkdown-samples/shapes.png) followed by more text](host:split)\n\n| Heading | Link |\n| --- | --- |\n| Cell | [Table link](host:table) |\n\n```text\nHost code actions remain in the focus chain.\n```\n\n<https://example.invalid> and [last link](host:last).\n" },
        { key: "syntax", title: "Syntax highlighting", source: "# Syntax highlighting\n\nOpen Style controls and check backend availability. If unavailable, launch task demo-highlighted (requires KF6SyntaxHighlighting). Enable Syntax colors when available. Try both palettes and edit incomplete code.\n\n```cpp\n/* state across\n   multiple lines */\nconst QString greeting = \"Hello 😀\";\nint count = 42;\n```\n\n```py\ndef greet(name):\n    print(f\"Hello {name}\")\n```\n\n```qml\nimport QtQuick\nItem { property string label: \"hello\" }\n```\n\n```bash\necho \"$HOME\" # comment\n```\n\n```json\n{\"answer\": 42, \"ready\": true}\n```\n\n```js\nfunction hello() { return \"world\"; }\n```\n\n```unknown\nThis source stays plain.\n```\n" },
        { key: "math", title: "Native block math", source: "# Native block math\n\nEnable Native math and close Find to see formulas. Document selection selects each rendered formula as one object; Find shows selectable TeX source.\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}+\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}\n$$\n\n```math\n\\sum_{i=0}^{n}i + \\int_0^1 x dx\n```\n\n> $$\n> \\begin{pmatrix}a&b\\\\c&d\\end{pmatrix}\n> $$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a&=b+c\\\\d&=e+f\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n```math\n\\unsupported{x}\n```\n" },
        { key: "scrolling", title: "Nested code scrolling", source: "# Nested code scrolling\n\nOpen Style controls: enable Limit code height and disable Wrap code. Scroll the document until the tall block is visible. Scroll inside it to each edge, continue into the document, then reverse direction. Repeat with wheel and touchpad phases.\n\nSurrounding document content.\n\nSurrounding document content.\n\nSurrounding document content.\n\nSurrounding document content.\n\nSurrounding document content.\n\nSurrounding document content.\n\nSurrounding document content.\n\nSurrounding document content.\n\n```cpp\n// Row 01: wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content \n// Row 02: wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content \n// Row 03: wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content \n// Row 04: wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content \n// Row 05: wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content \n// Row 06: wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide source content wide sour